      children: "Let's be honest: most software architecture documents are outdated the moment they are approved. They look impressive, full of diagrams, boxes, arrows, and confident claims about scalability, performance, and future-proofing. But two sprints later, reality has diverged. A “temporary” workaround became permanent. A critical dependency changed. A decision made under pressure never made it back into the document. The result is an architecture document that technically exists but is practically useless."
